The approach of the Smart Study Planner is to develop an AI and Machine Learning-based system that creates a personalized study schedule according to the individual needs of a student.
The system collects important information such as previous marks, subject difficulty, days remaining for examinations, available study hours, and current study progress.
The collected data is preprocessed and converted into a suitable format for the machine learning model. A Random Forest classification algorithm is used to analyze these factors and
predict the priority of each subject as High, Medium, or Low. 
Based on the predicted priorities, the system allocates available study time to different subjects and generates a daily or weekly study plan.
The system can also track completed study sessions and update future recommendations according to the student's progress.
The findings of the Smart Study Planner show that a personalized and data-driven study schedule can help students organize their preparation more effectively.
The system identifies subjects that require greater attention by considering factors such as low previous marks, higher difficulty, limited preparation time, and incomplete progress.
It gives higher priority to subjects that need more focus and helps distribute available study hours accordingly.
The project also demonstrates how Machine Learning can be used to classify study priorities instead of relying only on a fixed timetable.
Overall, the system can support better time management, consistent study habits, and focused preparation, while future improvements can include larger datasets, automatic schedule
adjustment, reminders, and more advanced recommendation techniques.
